  "id": "COMPOUND:26367 - PROTEIN:5702",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex but consistent relationship between CID 127037596 and CCF-STTG1, mediated through multiple targets. The drug CID 127037596 is shown to interact with CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, which in turn is targeted by several compounds, including (3aR,6S,6aR)-3,6-bis(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan and 6'-O-Z-Para-Methoxycinnamoylharpagide. These compounds are all implicated in targeting CCF-STTG1, indicating a potential pathway where CID 127037596 may influence the activity of these intermediates, which ultimately affect CCF-STTG1. The evidence suggests that CID 127037596 may act as a modulator of the target pathway, possibly through a direct or indirect interaction with the enzyme or its downstream targets. The consistent presence of these targets across different compounds supports the idea that CID 127037596 is involved in a broader biological process that involves the regulation of CCF-STTG1.",
